# Impossible OS user-mode test manifest
# =====================================
#
# Deployed by `make userland` to C:\tests\usermode.manifest.
# Read by the kernel-side launcher in src/kernel/test/test_usermode.c
# (TODO-04 §3 + §4 + §8). One filename per line, `#` starts a comment,
# blank lines are ignored. Order in this file is the priority order
# WITHIN a phase -- the launcher runs smokes (phase 0) then non-smokes
# (phase 1), so a smoke listed below a correctness test still runs first.
#
# §8 test-type taxonomy: the type is inferred from the filename prefix
#   test_smoke_*.exe   -> UTEST_TYPE_SMOKE       (phase 0; FAIL aborts run)
#   test_stress_*.exe  -> UTEST_TYPE_STRESS      (phase 1; looped stress_iters times)
#   test_perf_*.exe    -> UTEST_TYPE_PERF        (phase 1; emits [PERF] lines)
#   anything else      -> UTEST_TYPE_CORRECTNESS (phase 1; default)
# An optional `type=<name>` attribute on the line overrides the
# filename-derived default, e.g.:
#   test_foo.exe type=smoke     # force `test_foo.exe` into the smoke phase
#
# To restrict the run to ONE binary, set `utest_filter=test_foo.exe`
# in boot.conf (TODO-04 §4). Glob matching is supported: `test_smoke_*.exe`.

# §8 smoke phase -- one fast-fail gate for catastrophic boot regressions.
test_smoke_boot.exe

# -17 fast-path transport probes (gs:TEB, KUSD, syscall->SSDT).
# Runs early in the correctness phase so a broken ring-3 transition
# surfaces as FAIL on this binary, not as a silent hang in a later
# test that depends on any of the three fast paths. Exit code is a
# bitmap of failing probes (0 = all PASS); launcher reports the
# bitmap in its verdict line.
test_fastpath.exe

# -19 3-way transport fuzz (1000 iters each of INT 0x80 / SYSCALL /
# INT 0x2E calling NtClose(INVALID_HANDLE)). Any transport-level
# regression surfaces as FAIL on THIS binary with the specific
# iter + transport in the UTEST line; §19 transition ring captures
# the last 64 ring-3 crossings at the next panic for replay.
test_fastpath_fuzz.exe

# §1 harness self-test + correctness suites.
test_harness_smoke.exe
test_syscall.exe
test_libc.exe
test_ipc.exe
# test_process.exe forks eight children: three for fork/exec/kill and five for
# the exec commit-point lifecycle (post-commit termination, injected kmalloc
# OOM, oversized argv, the allocation-depth sweep, injected PMM OOM).
# Tell the launcher's pre-flight budget check so fork-heavy binaries
# count for 1 (launcher task) + 8 (forked children) = 9 slots. Keep this in
# step with the TASK-SLOT BUDGET comment at the top of test_process.c: a stale
# value here reports capacity the run does not have, and the binary then
# exhausts TASK_MAX and destabilises whatever runs after it.
test_process.exe expects_tasks=9
test_fileio.exe
test_win32.exe
# §15 binary-format loader coverage: one binary per registered format.
# Launcher emits `UTEST: <name>: format=<NAME>` before the verdict so a
# regression that silently routes the wrong loader surfaces even when
# the binary exits 0. ELF + EIF target USER_ELF_BASE (0x800000) via
# the per-process cr3's pre-split PT; PE targets its ImageBase via
# vmm_map_page which now propagates User at every intermediate
# table level (fix in src/kernel/mm/vmm.c get_or_create_table,
# 2026-04-22). Three-format coverage runs here as a unit so a
# kernel regression in any loader surfaces on the same boot.
test_loader_elf.exe
test_loader_pe.exe
test_loader_eif.exe
# Forks one child per kmalloc-backed exec site probe (2), one disarmed
# control fork for the fork-PML4 site probe (1), plus itself. The fork that
# the PML4 site REFUSES consumes no slot, because task_fork now fails closed
# before num_tasks++ publishes the child. PIDs are allocated monotonically
# and task_cleanup does not return slots, so the budget must name all four or
# the launcher's TASK_MAX pre-flight undercounts and a later stress test
# fails without the capacity warning.
test_faultinject.exe expects_tasks=4

# §8 stress + perf phase -- run after all correctness passes.
test_stress_libc.exe
test_perf_syscall.exe
